==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Unclear, but likely from {{der|en|kw|porth||harbor}} + {{m|kw|bugel||shepherd}}, with the latter element either influenced by {{noncog|en|beagle}} or in fact formed from it, with only the first element truly being from Cornish.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}
[[Image:Lanas u0.gif|right|thumb|A '''porbeagle'''.]]

# A large [[pelagic]] predatory [[shark]], {{taxfmt|Lamna nasus|species}}, of the [[Atlantic]].
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The Book of Sharks|author={{w|Richard Ellis (biologist)|Richard Ellis}}|year=1983|publisher=Knopf|ISBN=0679722106|passage=In English waters, the '''porbeagle''' is considered the premier shark to catch, but in other parts of the world it is considered a nuisance, or at best a poor substitute for its more glamorous relative, the mako.|page=59}}

